{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957927-just-for-fun-tommy-wiseau-in-the-chronicles-of-darkness","id":957927,"title":"Just for Fun- Tommy Wiseau in the Chronicles of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-25T16:55:08-07:00","id":957927,"title":"Just for Fun- Tommy Wiseau in the Chronicles of Darkness","content":"So in reference to something that got brought up in another thread, I decided to create a thread dedicated to a very silly topic: trying to work out splats from all game lines for infamous film director Tommy Wiseau. Any and all takers welcome. Suggestions can be as silly or logical as you want them to be. <br /> <br /> I'll get the ball rolling by proposing that Mr. Wiseau is a Nosferatu of the Ordo Dracul, with mastery of the Coil of the Ascendent. The Nosferatu explains his strange mannerisms and seeming disconnect from normal behavioral cues: it's the Lonely Curse manifesting itself as uncanny awkwardness. &quot;The Room&quot; was actually part of his Great Work: he <i>intentionally </i>set out to make it bad, so that he could study mortals' reaction to it. Imagine his surprise when people didn't simply hate it, but came to worship it as a masterpiece of unintentionally hilarious cinema.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T17:46:28-07:00","id":957953,"title":"","content":"He absolutely has to be a Demon with a phenomenally shitty Cover. People have tried to find where he was born to no avail, and he's said he's from several places. His inexplicable actions and utter lack of understanding of human customs are the desparate attempts of a glitched alien program trying to fit in, and his references to &quot;Planet Tommy&quot; are a confused thought of Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T19:34:36-07:00","id":958006,"title":"","content":"Tommy Wiseau is clearly a Promethean. The Room was his attempt at studying Human interactions, without really understanding them. I'd guess he's an Osiran, judging from what I know of the Room's creation.<br /> I remember that I couldn't help but think of Wiseau when going over Second Edition. There was something somewhere in there to the tune of &quot;Some Prometheans are fed up with this world and it's tearing them apart&quot; that made me suddenly realise it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T20:23:17-07:00","id":958023,"title":"","content":"Tommy Wisesu is an iron master werewolf born to two predator king parents, meaning he was raised as a feral child and thus doesn't humans that well. The room was an attempt to learn more about civilized people, and thus his new preferred prey that didn't work out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T02:56:44-07:00","id":958127,"title":"","content":"If you read Greg Sestero's wonderful book about the making of <i>The Room</i>, you definitely get the sense that some Disquiet is setting in. But we all know what happens when one completes one's Magnum Opus...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T11:13:22-07:00","id":962385,"title":"","content":"While I've always thought of him as a perfect Promethean, there's so much else to explore. <br /> <br /> He's been compared to a vampire, a mummy, and an alien- and he would be perfect as a Mummy or an exiled Gentry (seriously, that would explain so much). <br /> <br /> He's also a surprisingly good fit as a Mage or Genius, if you've read The Disaster Artist. His entire life has basically been about staring down reality and making it blink first. He has this aura of inexorable, causality-warping willpower around him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":